Z||000009||Eric||04-03-2000||05:31 PM||||That's nothing.  I went to a car race a couple weekends ago in Dallas where Vipers Corvettes and Cobras congrigated to rip it up on a private race track.  Talk about if rice boys won the lottery, jeez.  About half the Vipers had full ground effect packages with huge racing style, like the above, wings.  I got some great pictures of a damaged front air dam on one of these Vipers.  This funky thing was barely an inch off the ground, so when he spun if off the track at like 80mph or something, he knocked a bunch of the paint off it.  It must have been carbon fiber because it was still pretty much intact.  Of course a rice boy would have opted for the cheaper fiberglass.  Come to think of it, these guys were nothing like rice boys.  Most of the Vipers could run 11s in the quarter in the 120-140 mph range on street tires.  There was one RX7 there with funky moldings and weird rims, but he was running 12's at almost 120mph.  ||||reg||1
